eks, peaking at $35.02 and pulling back 31% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jan 31, 2025 it closed at $37.28, its first close above the base high of $35.02. Volume that day was 19.7M shares, 1.92x the prior 10-day average of 10.2M. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $68.74, and the chart ends at $34.75.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}